            {
                "entry_id": "8e64cdec-c679-32a0-b356-afdce2da574f",
                "word": "Shinto",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71e6ad7a-031d-34b4-94a4-448478f6b383",
                        "entry_id": "8e64cdec-c679-32a0-b356-afdce2da574f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Formerly the state religion of Japan, a type of animism involving the worship of ancestors and nature spirits."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "19d4766e-9140-49fb-96d5-1647009335f9",
                                "sense_id": "71e6ad7a-031d-34b4-94a4-448478f6b383",
                                "text": "The number of Shinto deities is very great. The Yengishiki enumerates 3,132 officially recognized shrines, and although the same Gods are reckoned more than once, as being worshipped in different places, still their name is legion."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe9522ca-7577-456b-ae33-64acb06240e2",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e64cdec-c679-32a0-b356-afdce2da574f",
                        "source_sense_id": "71e6ad7a-031d-34b4-94a4-448478f6b383",
                        "source_sense_description": "religion",
                        "target_lang_word": "šintoismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "šintoismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "86513f16-a0a3-3a82-b53c-54c2aeed5666",
                                        "entry_id": "e8d6ddca-6b1b-3d54-afdd-7e2ba62d7ee7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "původní japonské náboženství"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdafd8da-ab3f-46bc-b7aa-cc455c1a615f",
                                                "sense_id": "86513f16-a0a3-3a82-b53c-54c2aeed5666",
                                                "text": "Šogunové neměli právo, proměniti je v chrámy buddhistické anebo vedle šintoské bohoslužby zavésti buddhistickou. Šintoismus byl od starodávna náboženstvím mikadovým, tedy státním."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7b7cd1a-2c09-476c-bcd6-9ced0da487a6",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e64cdec-c679-32a0-b356-afdce2da574f",
                        "source_sense_id": "71e6ad7a-031d-34b4-94a4-448478f6b383",
                        "source_sense_description": "religion",
                        "target_lang_word": "Shintoïsme",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f75c209d-5d29-45f2-8d48-cda37adc35ce",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e64cdec-c679-32a0-b356-afdce2da574f",
                        "source_sense_id": "71e6ad7a-031d-34b4-94a4-448478f6b383",
                        "source_sense_description": "religion",
                        "target_lang_word": "shintoïsme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shintoïsme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40ab9a7e-e026-3fd1-bf83-f10a9deb6efe",
                                        "entry_id": "90094f4c-6fa4-3c90-bddf-fec1469e8351",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Religion animiste du Japon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e87e31b-6b3b-475e-8c44-6645c5b1c09e",
                                                "sense_id": "40ab9a7e-e026-3fd1-bf83-f10a9deb6efe",
                                                "text": "On sait que la religion des shintos ou shintoïsme consiste dans le culte d’une divinité suprême et de demi-dieux ou héros ; elle enseigne que les âmes des hommes vertueux iront habiter les régions lumineuses au seuil desquelles le Japon est placé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f45c7b7c-998f-4c13-9bf2-b21f5cca790b",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e64cdec-c679-32a0-b356-afdce2da574f",
                        "source_sense_id": "71e6ad7a-031d-34b4-94a4-448478f6b383",
                        "source_sense_description": "religion",
                        "target_lang_word": "shinto",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shinto",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bba27e0c-263a-38b1-bf33-d5ee852ff78c",
                                        "entry_id": "d40f1dbe-6003-32c8-a318-f164571bf4e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relatif au shintoïsme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eecbed58-d366-4b83-b523-adc1ff80e6bd",
                                                "sense_id": "bba27e0c-263a-38b1-bf33-d5ee852ff78c",
                                                "text": "Car les sanctuaires shinto sont aussi des lieux de vie, de marchés, de fêtes, de promenades, au cœur de la vie japonaise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shinto",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbfb7098-8d96-3a4b-a44b-12e4f126f87d",
                                        "entry_id": "651b4f10-efbb-3cb3-bc58-92ed5c6d6a61",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Shintoïsme, religion fondamentale la plus ancienne du Japon, mélange d’animisme et de chamanisme, essentiellement polythéiste."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a82f4cb0-6405-4607-bb5c-ab82ca5802fb",
                                                "sense_id": "fbfb7098-8d96-3a4b-a44b-12e4f126f87d",
                                                "text": "Le shintoïsme ou shinto est le « chemin vers les dieux » : ce terme explique la spécialiste des jardins japonais Danielle Elisseeff, recouvre une sorte d’émerveillement mêlé de crainte devant la nature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7cc7fa3-0a65-4f4a-96d8-e55dcd6238db",
                                                "sense_id": "fbfb7098-8d96-3a4b-a44b-12e4f126f87d",
                                                "text": "Les origines du shinto remontent très loin dans le passé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c0b90c98-37d9-4ecf-84aa-dbec8a695c0d",
